Careful: the oldString "assert.equal(res.status, 422); ... ATIVIDADE_JA_INICIADA" — appears in both C25 and C26! C25 ends with:

```
      assert.equal(res.status, 422);
      const corpo = await res.json();
      assert.equal(corpo.erro, 'ATIVIDADE_JA_INICIADA');
    });
```

and C26 ends with the same + `\n  });\n});`. The oldString included `    });\n  });\n});` — only C26 is followed by describe-close and file-close. C25 is followed by blank line + `it('Critério 26...`. So unique match — edit succeeded (no error). Good.

Run test — expect red (inscriptions still active after activity cancel).

Red. Implement R11: in `atividadeService.cancelarAtividade`, after `atv.isCancelada = true`, call a function from inscricaoService to cancel active inscriptions of that activity.

Circular import: atividadeService ← inscricaoService (already imports obterAtividadeBrutaPorId). Adding reverse import. ESM circular with function declarations should work.

Add to inscricaoService:
```js
// R11: cancelamento da atividade propaga para inscrições ativas
export function cancelarInscricoesDaAtividade(atividadeId) {
  for (const insc of inscricoesStore) {
    if (insc.atividadeId === atividadeId && STATUS_ATIVOS.includes(insc.status)) {
      insc.status = 'cancelada';
    }
  }
}
```

Do we need to sync counters? Activity is cancelled — ocupadas should become 0 (all confirmadas/convocadas became cancelada). R4 observável em GET /atividades. Cancelled activity counters: spec doesn't explicitly say, but "deixa de ocupar vaga" — yes, sync counters. sincronizarContadores needs the atv object — can do inside atividadeService call site or inside the function via obterAtividadeBrutaPorId (already imported). Do it in inscricaoService after loop.

In atividadeService.cancelarAtividade, after `atv.isCancelada = true`:
```js
cancelarInscricoesDaAtividade(id);
```

Import: `import { cancelarInscricoesDaAtividade } from './inscricaoService.js';` — circular. To be safe against TDZ issues, since both are function declarations used only at call time (not module init), it works.

