parts.text:
Red as expected. Now implement minimal for C16:

1. `convocarProximoDaFila(atv, agora)`: if vagasRestantes > 0 and there's em_espera → first em_espera becomes convocada with `convocadaEm = agora`; and R8: only if agora < encerramentoMs (C16 is before encerr — fine either way, but R8 check needed for C21 later; minimal for C16 could skip window check... C21 next-ish. Skill says minimal — but convocation without window check then C21 red later adding check is proper TDD. I'll do minimal: no window check yet? Actually C21 will be written soon; order: implement convocation for C16, then C20/C19 assert convocadaAte derivation, then C21 adds prohibition.

For C16, convocadaAte must be rendered: formatarInscricao computes it when status convocada: min(convocadaEm + 2h, encerramento). That's R8 derivation — needed already for C16 assertion (convocadaAte filled with exact value = +2h since far from encerr). So implement derivation now (covers C20 too when written).

Minimal now:
- store `convocadaEm: agora` when convocating
- formatarInscricao: if convocada → convocadaAte = iso(min(parse(convocadaEm)+2h, encerramentoMs(atv)))

ISO format: test expects '2026-10-13T11:00:00-03:00'. RelogioService returns agora as stored — default '2026-10-13T09:00:00-03:00'. +2h → need to produce same format with -03:00. Using Date arithmetic: new Date('2026-10-13T09:00:00-03:00') → ms → +2h → toISOString() gives '2026-10-13T14:00:00.000Z'. Test expects '-03:00' format. Contract says "API pode responder em qualquer fuso; o juiz compara o instante, não o texto." But MY test asserts exact text '2026-10-13T11:00:00-03:00'. Per contract, any ISO with equivalent instant is fine — I should assert instant equivalence instead of exact text? The test is mine; judge compares instante. Better to compare with Date.parse equality:

assert.equal(Date.parse(corpo.convocadaAte), Date.parse('2026-10-13T11:00:00-03:00'));

But criadaEm test earlier asserted exact text '2026-10-13T09:00:00-03:00' (fatia 1) — that works because we store the string as given.

For convocadaAte derived: easiest to produce text in same fuso -03:00. Compute: minMs of (convocadaEmMs + 2h, encerramentoMs). Format with -03:00 offset: take ms, subtract? -03:00 means local = UTC-3, so formatted = new Date(ms - 3*3600e3).toISOString().replace('Z','') minus ms precision → '2026-10-13T11:00:00.000' → strip .000 → '2026-10-13T11:00:00-03:00'.

Helper:
```js
function formatarIsoMenos3(ms) {
  const d = new Date(ms - 3 * 3600 * 1000);
  return d.toISOString().replace(/\.\d{3}Z$/, '-03:00');
}
```
Careful: ms-3h then toISOString (UTC) gives the wall clock in -03:00 as if UTC. Yes: 14:00Z - 3h = 11:00Z → '2026-10-13T11:00:00.000Z' → '2026-10-13T11:00:00-03:00'. Correct.

But wait — criadaEm comes from relógio which stores user-provided text. convocadaEm = agora (text from relógio, e.g. '2026-10-19T11:00:00-03:00'). Fine.

Alternatively simpler: my test could use Date.parse comparison (judge does that). Keep exact-text for determinism with -03:00 helper. Hmm, but what if clock set to 'Z' format in another test (C19 etc.)? I'll set clocks in -03:00 in tests. Encerramento from encontros also -03:00. min of two -03:00 instants → helper outputs -03:00 text. Good.

Also where to trigger convocation: in cancelarInscricao after sync counters, if the cancelled status was confirmada or convocada (freed slot) → convocarProximo. R7a: "cancelamento de inscrição confirmada ou convocada que libera a vaga". Cancel em_espera → no convocation.

Minimal for C16: after cancel, call convocarProximo when freed (cancelled was confirmada/convocada).

```js
const liberouVaga = insc.status === 'confirmada' || insc.status === 'convocada';
insc.status = 'cancelada';
if (atv) sincronizarContadores(atv);
if (liberouVaga && atv) convocarProximo(atv, agora);
```

convocarProximo:
```js
function convocarProximo(atv, agora) {
  if (new Date(agora).getTime() >= encerramentoMs(atv)) return; // R8 — add now? C21 needs it; adding now makes C21 green later. Minimal for C16 doesn't need. I'll add without R8 check now? No — adding R8 check now is "implementing next rule". Skip for now; C21 cycle adds it. Actually wait: without R8 check, C16 works. C21 later: cancel after encerramento → currently would convocate → red → then add check. Proper TDD. OK skip check now.

  const vagasLivres = Math.max(0, atv.vagas - contarOcupadas(atv.id));
  if (vagasLivres <= 0) return;
  const prox = inscricoesStore.find(i => i.atividadeId === atv.id && i.status === 'em_espera');
  if (!prox) return;
  prox.status = 'convocada';
  prox.convocadaEm = agora;
  sincronizarContadores(atv);
}
```
One per trigger ("uma vaga por vez") — single call, no loop. For PATCH +N, loop at call site or loop inside? C17 tests single increase. Spec "uma vag por vez"... for a +3 PATCH with 3 waiting, intuitively all 3 convocated. I'll loop inside: while vagas>0 && fila. Hmm but then "convoca-se o primeiro da fila, uma vaga por vez" reads like each iteration convocates the first — a while loop convocates first each time. I'll do the while loop — it matches "sempre que vagasRestantes > 0 e houver fila".

Wait, but careful: blind convocation + while loop. Cancel of 1 confirmada frees 1 slot → loop runs once (vagasLivres becomes 0 after one convocada). Same outcome. PATCH +3 →3 convocadas. Good.

formatarInscricao convocadaAte:
```js
let convocadaAte = null;
if (insc.status === 'convocada') {
  const atv = obterAtividadeBrutaPorId(insc.atividadeId);
  const prazoMs = Math.min(Date.parse(insc.convocadaEm) + 2*3600*1000, atv ? encerramentoMs(atv) : Infinity);
  convocadaAte = formatarIsoMenos3(prazoMs);
}
```

Also posicaoNaEspera: convocada → null (already: only em_espera gets position).

Implement now.

