parts.text:
Now implement R16 / C42. Verified by inspection of static files: listing must expose "inscrever, cancelar e confirmar" operations and a "minhas inscrições" section with status and posicaoNaEspera.

Plan:
1. index.html: add section "Minhas Inscrições" (`#minhas-inscricoes`) with a container list; also add more participant users to select? The select has org-ana, org-bruno, p-carla. Fine (participants only see their own).

2. app.js:
   - After loading activities, also load `GET /inscricoes` for current user and map by atividadeId.
   - In activity card (listing): show operation button depending on user + inscription state:
     - participant + no active inscription (or none): "Inscrever" button → POST /atividades/:id/inscricoes
     - participant + active inscription (confirmada/em_espera/convocada): "Cancelar" button → POST /inscricoes/:id/cancelamento
     - participant + convocada: "Confirmar" button → POST /inscricoes/:id/confirmacao - org: no inscrever/cancelar/confirmar buttons (403).
   - "Minhas inscrições" section: table/cards listing user's inscriptions with atividade title, status badge, posicaoNaEspera (when applicable). For org, hide section or show nothing? R16: "visualizar a seção minhas inscrições" — for participante. Org gets all via API; UI section is for the participant. Show only for participants (or show for org with all? Spec says participante). I'll show section only for participants.
   - Buttons stopPropagation so card click (modal) still works.
   - After operations: reload activities + minhas inscrições; show feedback (alert).

Also modal could get the same actions — R16 says "a partir da listagem de atividades: inscrever-se, cancelar a inscrição e confirmar convocação" — listing-level buttons suffice.

Keep simple and consistent with existing style. Status badges: add CSS for confirmada, em_espera, convocada, cancelada, expirada.

Implementation details in renderizarAtividades: needs inscricoes map. Load both in a combined refresh function:

```js
let minhasInscricoes = [];

async function carregarMinhasInscricoes() {
  const res = await fetch('/inscricoes', { headers: getHeaders() });
  if (res.ok) minhasInscricoes = await res.json(); else minhasInscricoes = [];
  renderizarMinhasInscricoes();
}

function renderizarMinhasInscricoes() { ... }
```

For org: section hidden (like org-section inverse). Also inscrever buttons only for participants.

Statuses active: confirmada, em_espera, convocada → show Cancelar; convocada → also Confirmar; cancelada/expirada → show Inscrever (re-inscrição allowed) — but only if activity not started etc.; UI shows button, API rejects with error shown.

Card button handling:

```js
function acaoInscricaoHtml(atv, insc) {
  if (usuarioSelect.value.startsWith('org-')) return '';
  if (!insc || insc.status === 'cancelada' || insc.status === 'expirada') {
    return `<button class="btn primary btn-inscrever" data-id="${atv.id}">Inscrever</button>`;
  }
  let html = `<button class="btn secondary btn-cancelar-insc" data-insc="${insc.id}">Cancelar</button>`;
  if (insc.status === 'convocada') {
    html = `<button class="btn primary btn-confirmar-insc" data-insc="${insc.id}">Confirmar</button>` + html;
  }
  return html;
}
```

Event listeners after innerHTML: card.querySelector('.btn-inscrever')?.addEventListener...

Note: buttons inside card with click → open modal: use e.stopPropagation().

Renderização da inscrição no card: maybe show status badge on card. R16 requires the section to show status and posicaoNaEspera — the section handles that.

Minhas inscrições render:

```html
<section id="minhas-inscricoes" class="card hidden">
  <h2>Minhas Inscrições</h2>
  <div id="inscricoes-lista"><p class="loading">…</p></div>
</section>
```

Render rows: atividade titulo (map from loaded atividades — need atividades cache), status badge, posição when em_espera: `#${posicaoNaEspera}`, convocadaAte maybe. Buttons cancel/confirm here too? R16 says listing exposes operations; section shows status/posicao. Adding cancel/confirm buttons in section is a bonus — keep section informative with status + posicao; operations on activity listing.

Cache atividades: store `let atividadesCache = []` in carregarAtividades.

Reload orchestration:

```js
async function recarregar() {
  await Promise.all([carregarAtividades(), carregarMinhasInscricoes()]);
}
```

carregarAtividades sets grid; minhas sets section.

On user change: atualizarPermissoesUI (show/hide minhas section based on participant), carregarAtividades + carregarMinhasInscricoes.

Feedback: reuse apiErrorAlert? That's inside org form. Add a global alert at top of main? Use a toast-ish div `#feedback-alert` above grade section. Or alert() for simplicity? Existing style uses modal alerts. I'll add a global `#feedback` alert div in main before grade section, with helper mostrarFeedback(msg, tipo).

Error display: show `[ERRO] mensagem` from API.

Write the code now. Also update title/subtitle to mention M2? Title says "M1: Grade". Update subtitle to "M1/M2 — Grade e Inscrições". Minor, fine.

CSS: add badges for statuses + button sizes in cards; `.atividade-acoes` container; `.inscricao-item` rows in section.

TDD aspect: C42 is verified by inspection (not HTTP test). Skill says test must fail first — for R16 the spec itself says inspection of static files. So: implement files, then inspect (read) to confirm. Optionally add a test? Spec C42: "verificado por inspeção dos arquivos estáticos, não por teste HTTP". So no test. Implement + inspect + run suite (must stay green) + commit.

Write index.html edits.

